[#:seon.task{:name "slow-explanation-blames-the-agent-for-platform-time"
             :kind :function
             :intent "explain-slow tells the agent 'this is your defect' from a JVM-wide counter delta. The first (inc 1) on a new branch answered :ms 1307 with the OVER ONE SECOND text while its lines named `seon.sci.eval/acquire!` 1290 ms and derive-base-ctx 1075 ms: Seon's program acquisition inside the arm, not the agent's form. The window is every cell in the JVM (a 4.5 s window around one form held 35 evaluations and 57 transactions of other lanes), so no per-operation attribution is correct under concurrency; the evaluation path appends the lines to `:seon.cluster.eval/output`, so the reply's :out shows text the form never printed. The same begin/explain duplicate serves MCP JVM mode, test members and publication. Attribute per operation (a window carried by the kernel arm), judge the agent on its own time only, and deliver platform time as a fault to root. Same class (stability sweep 2026-09-27): an admitted defn's reply carried :out 'No example test gates stab.nested/stab-inc; add a deftest ...' (seon.test.accretion advisories, accretion.clj ~311-315), guidance prose in the output stream instead of a data key. The per-arm slow list that replaces the JVM-wide window is task seon.repl/a-slow-reply-names-nothing (seon.repl). Done when :out holds only what the form printed, guidance and slow calls arrive as reply keys, and a concurrent lane's work is never named in another agent's reply."
             :must-read #{seon.profile/begin seon.profile/explain seon.profile/explain-slow}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/eval-feedback-design-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/stability-sweep-2026-09-27.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/perf-audit-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "scope-wrappers-report-callback-time-as-work"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Higher-order scope wrappers are armed with ordinary profile cells, so their inclusive time is their callback's, waits included. `seon.flow/graph-executor` (flow.clj:96) runs every Flow proc thread's whole life inside `seon.schema/call-with-projection-state`: the previous default reported it 5,223,273 ms total, max 754,816 ms, x269, which is proc threads blocked on channels, not work. call-with-projection (x51-x487), call-with-forms and `seon.db/call-with-custody` rank the same way and lead every over-one-second list. A reader of by-total/over-second takes them for costs. Rank self-evident work: omit or mark functions whose declared input includes a callback, or report the callee instead."
             :must-read #{seon.profile/top seon.profile/explain seon.schema/call-with-projection-state}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/perf-boot-opus-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/stability-sweep-2026-09-27.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/perf-audit-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "call-counters-are-jvm-wide-so-counting-tests-race"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Tests that count calls now read seon.profile's per-definition counters (`seon.test-support/armed-counts`, armed-calls) instead of redefining the Var, which no longer breaks other tests; but a LongAdder counts every thread, so a concurrent member calling the same Var (`seon.sci.kernel/invoke`, `seon.schema/projection-from-database`, `seon.render/acquire-context!`) makes an exact count in another test red. Tests that filtered to their own thread (config-test sparse-file-reading, config-writer, db-test d/db) or by argument (retained counts per render symbol, web-test candidate-call-ids) stay redefinitions. Done when armed calls can be observed per scope, like `seon.db/*read-evidence-sink*` for reads (e.g. a bound call sink the armed wrapper appends to), armed-counts reads it, and two members counting the same Var concurrently each see only their own calls."
             :must-read #{seon.profile/begin seon.profile/explain seon.profile/cells}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/test-agents-concurrency-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "the-bracket-leaves-a-thread-local-entry-per-cell-on-every-thread"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`seon.profile/timed` restores a cell's entry with (.set entered prior), so an outermost exit sets nil and leaves the ThreadLocal's slot in that thread's ThreadLocalMap: a long-lived thread (the prepl, a Flow proc thread) holds one entry per cell it ever called (up to about 2,560), and each ThreadLocal.get probes that map. Measured 2026-09-28: the same bracket cost 40 to 52 ns per call on the prepl thread depending on which ThreadLocal instance it drew, and 40 to 41 ns on fresh threads. Done when an outermost exit removes its entry (or the entry lives in one per-thread structure) and the bracket costs the same on a long-lived thread as on a fresh one, measured parent against change."
             :must-read #{seon.profile/timed seon.profile/with-cell}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/health-recording-2026-09-28.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "reading-the-profile-cells-costs-3-ms"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`seon.profile/cells` builds a vector of every live cell (2,673) on each call: 2.9 ms, and summing each cell's total counter over it 2.5 ms (default 2026-09-28); a health report reads it live every time (the counters move with the read itself, so no key can hold it). Done when the report's candidates (definitions with a second of inclusive time) are found without touching every cell, e.g. from the stored judgments once they land."
             :must-read #{seon.profile/cells seon.profile/observation}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/task-census/evidence/health-page--RESUME.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "no-per-symbol-profile-and-zero-calls-reads-as-unmeasured"
             :kind :function
             :intent "There is no per-symbol profile function for an agent, and zero calls cannot be told from never measured. Done when a my.* call answers one symbol's calls, mean and max, and a symbol with no measurement answers a typed unknown while a measured zero answers zero."
             :must-read #{seon.profile/cell}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/task-census/evidence/repl-audit--read.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "reading-the-profile-validates-every-cell"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`seon.profile/cells` returns [:vector `:seon.profile/cell`] and its armed output check runs seven predicates (adder? x2, thread-local?, accumulator?, histogram?, throw-counts?, measured-mark?) on every live cell: one call costs 20,497 armed calls and 12 MB with 2,928 cells (default 2026-10-07). begin, explain, explain-slow, top and `seon.health/report` each read cells, so this is the producer of `seon.profile/histogram?` on the health top (4.97 M calls) and of 0.49-0.98 M calls of each sibling predicate in a 50 min session. Fix: the roster's members are cells by construction (cell is the only writer); check the cell once at `cell`, and declare the read's output by a schema that does not re-validate each member's JDK objects. Done when (`seon.profile/cells`) costs under 10 armed calls; regression: a profile test asserting the armed-call count of one cells read."
             :must-read #{seon.profile/cells seon.profile/cell seon.profile/begin}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/task-census/evidence/waste-rank--plus-1-2-armed-calls.edn"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "transaction-stamps-store-hot-and-repeated-sets-nothing-reads"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`seon.profile/transaction-observation` stamps every transaction over its call/ms threshold with `:seon.db.transaction/hot` (up to 20 [sym digest calls ms] tuples) and `:seon.db.transaction/repeated`; `seon.db/stamp-transaction` attaches them. No src reader exists (only seon.profile-test asserts them). A 17-test run-owned on a branch agent (default, 2026-10-07, db-watch lane) stamped 20+40 hot/repeated datoms (~6 KB of values) on its record-tx and 28 (~2.8 KB) on its request tx. Every stored fact names its consumer or is deleted: delete both attributes and their derivation (the explanation of a slow operation reads the live profile, not stored stamps), or name the consumer. Done when no transaction carries them and the per-test-run datom count (watch.clj :since-basis) drops accordingly."
             :must-read #{seon.profile/transaction-observation seon.db/stamp-transaction}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/db-watch/findings.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "begin-validates-every-cell-with-armed-predicates",
            :kind :function,
            :intent
            "`seon.profile/begin` says it calls no other armed function, but each call grows the entry counters of `seon.profile/adder?` by 5,320 and measured-mark?, accumulator?, thread-local?, histogram? by 2,660 each (2,660 live cells, default 2026-10-07): about 18,600 armed calls and 3.5 MB per mark, from its contracts validating every cell. A window measured with begin therefore counts the probe itself. Make the mark's own cost independent of armed validation of each cell. Proof: a deftest asserting two consecutive marks show zero armed entry growth.",
            :must-read #{seon.profile/begin},
            :evidence
            #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/plan-research/r-turn-notes.md"}}

 #:seon.task{:name "health-and-explain-rank-wrapper-chains-by-inclusive-time"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`seon.profile/summary` now ranks by self time (`:seon.profile/self-ms` on every observation), but `seon.profile/explain` (`:growths`, `:lines`) and `seon.health/report` (definitions with a second of inclusive time) still rank inclusive totals, so `seon.flow/in-world`, `seon.turn/phase` and `seon.schema/call-with-projection-state` lead runtime_status on 70 s of callback time (2026-10-08). Done when explain's growths carry self time ranked first and the health candidates name definitions by self time with their inclusive total beside it."
             :must-read #{seon.profile/explain seon.profile/observation seon.health/report}}
]
